# English Suite No. 2 in A minor, BWV 807: Bourree I (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: an energetic bourree in cut time, two beats to the bar,
# from a quarter upbeat. The theme is a trilled quarter-and-eighths
# figure (e d e f e d); most of the piece is driving eighth-note
# sequences over a bass in eighths or quarters. Firm and dancing, with
# the half-bar pulse always felt.
#
# Time signature: 2/2, 57 bars in the Mutopia score and in the MIDI,
# counting both endings of the first half: bar 24 is the first ending
# (three beats, then the upbeat back to bar 1), bar 25 the second
# ending (three beats, then the upbeat to B). Bar 57 is three beats.
# The MIDI plays the score once, both endings in a row, so play
# restores the order.
#
# Repeats: both halves repeated. About 7.5 KB.
#   play: upbeat to the first ending (0.75-24), the repeat (1-23), the
#   second ending and B (25-57.75), B again from its upbeat.
#   Performed bars: A 0.75-25, A repeat 25-48 (score x is x+24),
#   B 48-80.75 (score x is x+23), B repeat 80.75-113 (score x is x+55).
#
# Tempo: half note = 90, about 2:30 with repeats.
# Track times: Richard Egarr (harpsichord, Harmonia Mundi 2013), Bourree
# I on its own track, 2:27, about half = 91 with both repeats (confirmed
# from the Harmonia Mundi track list). Angela Hewitt (Hyperion) 4:04 and
# Andras Schiff (Decca) about 4:01 for Bourree I, II and I da capo on
# one track; they cannot be split. Glenn Gould (Sony) 1:26 for Bourree I
# alone, about 80 if without repeats (his plan not confirmed). 90
# follows Egarr: eighths 10 frames each, clear on the chip.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score):
#   1-4     A minor, the theme in the top over a bass in eighths.
#   5-8     the theme's figure in sequence; cadence in A minor (8).
#   9-14    broken-chord sequence falling through A minor, G, F#.
#   15-23   E minor, eighths in the top over a quarter bass; cadence in
#           E minor (23, and the endings 24, 25).
#   26-31   B: C major, moving to D minor (F, B flat, C sharp).
#   32-40   falling sequence in D minor; cadence in D minor (40-41).
#   42-49   the theme's figure returns, through A minor to a half close
#           on E (49).
#   50-54   rising sequence, each bar a step higher (C to A).
#   55-57   final cadence in A minor.
#
# Plan: each half full the first time, echoed on the repeat. In B the
# return of the theme's figure after the D minor cadence (score 42-49)
# steps down to mf, and the rising sequence (score 50) builds back to
# full. The final pass returns to full at the rising sequence.

pickup 4

tempo 90 2

play 0.75-24 1-23 25-57.75 25.75-57

dyn 1 f            # A first time
dyn 24.75 mp       # A repeat from its upbeat, an echo
broaden 48 0.95    # score 25: the E minor cadence before B
dyn 48.75 f        # B first time, from its upbeat
dyn 65 mf          # score 42-49: the theme's figure, a step down
ramp 73-77 f       # score 50-54: the rising sequence builds to full
broaden 80 0.95    # score 57: a breath before the B repeat
dyn 80.75 mp       # B repeat, an echo
ramp 105-109 f     # score 50-54: build to full for the close

rit 2 0.8          # the last two bars into the final A
